      "description": "Watch Rangers vs Jagiellonia highlights and goals from UEFA Europa League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 13, 2026. On August 13, 2026, the UEFA Europa League returned to the spotlight as Rangers faced off against Jagiellonia in a highly anticipated fixture. Both sets of fans filled the stadium with noise, anticipating a night of high-quality European football under the lights. Shankland Strikes Early The match ignited in the 19th minute when Rangers were awarded a penalty following sustained pressure. Lawrence Shankland stepped up to the spot and clinicaly dispatched his effort into the net, giving the home side an early lead. The remainder of the first half was a gritty affair, characterized by tactical battles in the midfield, as Jagiellonia struggled to find a way past a disciplined Scottish defense before the interval. Rising Tension and Tactical Changes The second half began with immediate intensity. Jagiellonia 's Taras Romanczuk received a yellow card just after the restart, signaling a more aggressive approach from the visitors. Rangers manager opted for a change at the break, bringing on Ross McCrorie to solidify the midfield. As the clock ticked past the hour mark, the game became increasingly physical, leading to another booking, this time for Bernardo Vital in the 63rd minute. Prelec Secures the Comeback The momentum shifted decisively in the 65th minute. Anders Klynge turned provider, delivering a perfect ball for Nik Prelec , who made no mistake in finding the target to level the score. Both managers turned to their benches to find a winner, with Cameron Devlin and Bojan Miovski joining the action for Rangers . Despite a frantic final period and seven minutes of stoppage time, neither side could find the decisive goal, resulting in a hard-fought draw that reflected the competitive nature of the contest."
